cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Vesuvius Uncertainty Bench"
message: >-
  If you use this software or the derived labels, please cite the EduceLab-Scrolls
  dataset (below) and acknowledge the Vesuvius Challenge as the source of the
  underlying scans and of the ink-detection model outputs from which the labels
  derive.
type: software
abstract: >-
  Tools, a benchmark and a provenance audit for ink detection in Herculaneum
  papyri above 100 keV: a surface renderer validated to correlation 1.00000 that
  fetches only the exact chunk shell a surface touches, derived ink-label sets at
  8.640 um/116 keV and 9.362 um/113 keV with a measured public-checkpoint
  ceiling, and line-periodicity judges whose false-positive rate is bounded on
  real substrate.
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Herculaneum
  - Vesuvius Challenge
  - virtual unwrapping
  - ink detection
  - X-ray micro-CT
  - benchmark
  - statistical validation
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      EduceLab-Scrolls: Verifiable Recovery of Text from Herculaneum Papyri
      using X-ray CT
    year: 2023
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:2304.02084"
    authors:
      - family-names: Parsons
        given-names: Stephen
      - family-names: Parker
        given-names: C. Seth
      - family-names: Chapman
        given-names: Christy
      - family-names: Hayashida
        given-names: Mami
      - family-names: Seales
        given-names: W. Brent
